# Ideamart Integration — Agent Instructions

> Portable entry point for Cursor, Windsurf, GitHub Copilot, Codex, Cline, Aider, Zed and any
> other agent that reads `AGENTS.md`. Claude Code and the Agent SDK use [SKILL.md](SKILL.md) —
> same content, skill frontmatter.

Ideamart is Dialog Axiata's telco platform for **Sri Lanka**, covering the operators Dialog,
Hutch (072 and 078) and Airtel. It exposes SMS, USSD, subscription management, mobile-account
charging and location as JSON-over-HTTPS APIs.

**Apply these instructions whenever the work involves Ideamart, IdeaPro, `api.ideamart.io`,
`tel:` MSISDN addressing, USSD menus, shortcode/keyword routing, subscriber base size,
direct carrier billing, or telco SMS in Sri Lanka.**

The platform is JSON over HTTPS, so **any language builds a complete integration** — write it
in whatever the host project already uses. Every endpoint is written out as a runnable curl,
with its parameters and its response defined, in
[references/13-curl-reference.md](references/13-curl-reference.md): translate the request into
the project's HTTP client and you have the call, whatever the language. Reference
implementations and code emitters exist for TypeScript/Node, Python, Java, Go, PHP and C# as a
convenience on top of that, and [references/11-any-stack.md](references/11-any-stack.md)
specifies the surrounding integration language-neutrally.

